@startuml Manifest Creation Process

' TARGET DESIGN (ADRs 0004, 0005, 0006, 0008; decisions P6, X3, X5, O36).
' Approval is no longer the fork that releases the paperwork: it signs off a vehicle's load, and the
' declarations are prepared and filed afterwards, manually by default. The code still implements the
' earlier version (approval refuses without an ENS, freezes the manifest, then hands off the GMR, the
' document and the ELO) until docs/plans/08 and docs/plans/15 merge. That version of this file is in
' git history at commit f659eed.
'
' Role-by-role detail: docs/process/00-end-to-end-overview.puml and docs/process/05.

title Manifest Creation Process
caption Target design. ADRs 0004, 0005, 0006, 0008. Detail in docs/process.

start

group Planning {

    :Truck List Created;
    ' Still the gate it always was: a manifest is proposed only against a published list.
    :Truck List Published;
    :Boxes Allocated to Vehicles;
    :Manifest Proposed;

    if (Administrator approves the load?) then (no)
        :Manifest Rejected;
        :Load fixed, proposed again;
    else (yes)
    endif

    :Manifest Approved (sign-off only);

}

group Declarations {

    ' The ENS comes first: the ELO pairs the crossing against its MRN. Filed outside Freedom by the
    ' Dispatcher, with the Ground Officer entering the consignee address (decisions X1, O32).
    fork
        :File ENS in ICS2 (outside Freedom);
        :Record ENS MRN;
        :File or record ELO (names the ENS MRN);
    fork again
        :File or record GMR;
    fork again
        :Prepare goods list per Receiver;
        :Receiver files it in Ukraine;
        :Record goods-list reference;
    end fork

    if (Load changed after filing?) then (yes)
        :Manifest back to Proposed;
        :Declarations stale: re-approve and re-declare;
    else (no)
    endif

}

group Execution {

    :Prepare Boxes;
    :Place Boxes in Bays;
    :Load Trucks;
    if (Every blocking requirement holds?) then (no)
        :Departure refused, with what is missing;
        stop
    else (yes)
    endif
    :Convoy Departs;

}

group Stock Ordering {

    fork
        :Update Truck Kit Stock;
    fork again
        :Update Merchandise Stock;
    end fork

}

end

@enduml
